35:       {name:'Zanzibar, Tanzania',short:'Zanzibar',emoji:'⛵',tag:'INDIAN OCEAN ISLANDS · TANZANIA',palette:['#f2d293','#398b81','#d27f5c','#65a5a0'],clues:['Kiswahili (Swahili) is widely spoken across the islands.','Stone Town reflects centuries of Indian Ocean exchange and layered histories.','Cloves and other spices have shaped parts of the islands’ trade and farming.'],fact:'Zanzibar’s culture reflects many histories and communities. No single food, language, or faith represents everyone.',contrast:'Compare: Zanzibar is an Indian Ocean archipelago with a distinct island history; mainland Tanzania is vast and regionally varied.'},
